THEN MFA must be enforced and access must be restricted to only those roles required for specific tasks.'}, {'id': 'SC-REQ-003', 'category': 'Operational', 'text': 'All systems involved in the software supply chain—such as version control, build tools, and artifact repositories—must log authentication attempts, configuration changes, and other anomalous events.', 'rationale': 'Logging and monitoring are essential for detecting and responding to attacks, particularly in complex supply chains where anomalous behavior may go unnoticed.', 'acceptance_criteria': 'GIVEN a system event (e.g., login, configuration change);
WHEN it occurs;
THEN a log entry must be generated and stored in a centralized SIEM or log aggregation system with sufficient depth and breadth to support incident response.'}, {'id': 'SC-REQ-004', 'category': 'Security', 'text': 'No credentials, including API keys or passwords, must be stored in source code repositories or transmitted in clear text.', 'rationale': 'Storing credentials in source code exposes them to unauthorized access and can lead to full compromise of the supply chain.', 'acceptance_criteria': 'GIVEN a source code repository;
WHEN a credential is attempted to be committed;
THEN the action must be rejected and an alert must be generated.'}]

[{'id': 'SEC-BUILD-01', 'category': 'Security', 'text': 'Build environments shall be ephemeral and isolated, using containerized or virtualized environments that are destroyed immediately after the build completes.', 'rationale': 'Ephemeral environments prevent attackers from reusing or compromising build environments through cache poisoning or code injection.', 'acceptance_criteria': 'GIVEN a build is initiated in a containerized environment;
WHEN the build completes;
THEN the environment is automatically terminated and no residual state or access is retained.'}, {'id': 'SEC-BUILD-02', 'category': 'Security', 'text': 'All build processes shall minimize or eliminate user-controllable parameters that can be modified during execution.', 'rationale': 'User-controllable parameters increase the risk of malicious input altering the build process, potentially introducing vulnerabilities.', 'acceptance_criteria': 'GIVEN a build process with user-controllable parameters;
WHEN a user attempts to modify a parameter;
THEN the build process shall reject the input or fail with a clear error message, and no build shall proceed with modified parameters.'}, {'id': 'SEC-BUILD-03', 'category': 'Security', 'text': 'Build provenance shall be generated using tools such as FRSCA or SLSA GitHub Generator and verified using SLSA Verifier.', 'rationale': 'Provenance ensures traceability and authenticity of the build process, enabling verification of integrity and origin.', 'acceptance_criteria': 'GIVEN a build process;
WHEN provenance is generated and stored;
THEN SLSA Verifier shall validate the provenance and report any inconsistencies or missing components.'}, {'id': 'SEC-DEPLOY-01', 'category': 'Security', 'text': 'The final binary output shall be scanned for exposed secrets, unauthorized components, and integrity violations using binary composition analysis.', 'rationale': 'Binary composition analysis helps detect vulnerabilities and unauthorized content that may have been introduced during the build or runtime.', 'acceptance_criteria': 'GIVEN a final binary;
WHEN scanned using a binary composition analysis tool;
THEN the scan shall detect any exposed secrets or unauthorized components and report findings to the deployment team.'}, {'id': 'SEC-MONITOR-01', 'category': 'Security', 'text': 'Deployed software shall be continuously monitored for vulnerabilities, including new vulnerabilities introduced via updates or newly disclosed in public sources.', 'rationale': 'Vulnerabilities in deployed software remain a risk even after deployment, and continuous monitoring ensures timely response.', 'acceptance_criteria': 'GIVEN a deployed software system;
WHEN a new vulnerability is discovered in a dependency or runtime component;
THEN an alert shall be generated and the system configuration shall be reviewed for insecure changes.'}]

[{'id': 'SEC-001', 'requirement': 'The IDPS shall perform network traffic analysis at the IP and transport layers to detect suspicious patterns and known attack signatures.', 'rationale': 'Supports detection of common threats such as port scans, TCP reset attacks, and protocol misuse based on established IDPS capabilities.', 'acceptance_criteria': 'GIVEN network traffic is captured at the IP and transport layers;
WHEN a known attack signature or suspicious pattern is detected;
THEN the IDPS shall generate an alert and initiate a blocking action within 10 seconds.'}, {'id': 'SEC-002', 'requirement': 'The IDPS shall support both signature-based and network behavior analysis (NBA) detection methods.', 'rationale': 'Signature-based detection provides known threat coverage; NBA enables detection of novel or unknown threats based on behavioral anomalies.', 'acceptance_criteria': 'GIVEN a network session with abnormal traffic patterns;
WHEN the IDPS detects a deviation from baseline behavior;
THEN it shall trigger a warning and initiate a review process within 5 minutes.'}, {'id': 'NON-001', 'requirement': 'The IDPS shall maintain logs of all detection events, actions taken, and system performance metrics for at least 90 days.', 'rationale': 'Logging is essential for incident response, forensic analysis, and compliance with logging and monitoring standards.', 'acceptance_criteria': 'GIVEN a detection event occurs;
WHEN the IDPS processes the event;
THEN a log entry shall be generated and stored in a secure, accessible location for at least 90 days.'}, {'id': 'SEC-003', 'requirement': 'The IDPS shall support integration with a Security Information and Event Management (SIEM) system via syslog or API for centralized monitoring and alerting.', 'rationale': 'Centralized monitoring improves visibility and enables correlation of events across multiple systems.', 'acceptance_criteria': 'GIVEN a detection event occurs;
WHEN the IDPS detects a security policy violation;
THEN it shall send a syslog message to the SIEM system within 2 seconds.'}]

[{'id': 'SEC-001', 'requirement': 'The system shall detect application-layer DoS attacks, such as slow HTTP attacks, by monitoring HTTP request patterns and identifying unusually slow or fragmented requests.', 'rationale': 'Slow HTTP attacks exhaust server resources by keeping connections open until data is fully delivered, leading to resource exhaustion and service unavailability. Detection is critical to prevent resource depletion.', 'acceptance_criteria': 'GIVEN a slow HTTP attack is launched against the web application;
WHEN the system monitors incoming HTTP requests;
THEN it shall detect requests with unusually low data transfer rates and trigger a mitigation response within 5 seconds.'}, {'id': 'SEC-002', 'requirement': 'The system shall detect and mitigate MAC flooding attacks by monitoring switch MAC table usage and triggering a fail-over mode when the table is exceeded by 90% of capacity.', 'rationale': 'MAC flooding attacks consume switch memory, leading to a fail-over state where all traffic is forwarded to all ports, causing data leakage and network disruption. Early detection prevents full network collapse.', 'acceptance_criteria': "GIVEN a MAC flooding attack is initiated;
WHEN the switch MAC table reaches 90% capacity;
THEN the system shall detect the anomaly and trigger a fail-over mode within 3 seconds, and log the event with a severity level of 'Critical'."}, {'id': 'SEC-003', 'requirement': 'The system shall detect ARP poisoning attacks by identifying spoofed ARP messages and blocking them using packet filtering technology.', 'rationale': 'ARP poisoning allows attackers to intercept or block traffic intended for legitimate devices, leading to denial of service on local network segments. Packet filtering can prevent such attacks from propagating.', 'acceptance_criteria': 'GIVEN a spoofed ARP message is sent to a legitimate device;
WHEN the system inspects incoming packets;
THEN it shall identify the spoofed message and block it, preventing it from reaching the target device.'}, {'id': 'PERF-001', 'requirement': 'The system shall maintain at least 99.9% availability during normal operations and under DoS attack conditions, with a maximum degradation of 10% in response time during an attack.', 'rationale': 'Availability is a core component of the CIA triad. The system must remain functional under attack conditions to ensure service continuity.', 'acceptance_criteria': 'GIVEN a DoS attack is active;
WHEN the system is under sustained attack;
THEN the service availability shall remain above 99.9%, and response time shall not exceed 100% of baseline performance.'}]

[{'id': 'VULN-REQ-01', 'category': 'Functional', 'text': 'The system shall allow researchers to submit vulnerability reports with a clear description, impact, affected versions, and a request for confidentiality.', 'rationale': 'Ensures researchers can provide detailed information while maintaining confidentiality, aligning with best practices in vulnerability disclosure.', 'acceptance_criteria': 'GIVEN a researcher submits a report with impact and affected versions;
