[{'id': 'SEC-001', 'requirement': 'The network infrastructure shall not hold state for unverified hosts to reduce the effectiveness of DoS attacks that exploit state exhaustion.', 'rationale': 'As per RFC 4732, holding state for unverified hosts can be exploited by attackers to simulate legitimate traffic and exhaust system resources.', 'acceptance_criteria': 'GIVEN a DoS attack using unverified hosts to simulate legitimate traffic;
WHEN the system is under attack;
THEN the system shall not maintain state for unverified hosts and shall respond with a timeout or rejection within 1 second.'}, {'id': 'SEC-002', 'requirement': 'The system shall implement graceful routing degradation to maintain service availability during routing protocol attacks or failures.', 'rationale': 'RFC 4732 recommends graceful routing degradation as a mitigation strategy to ensure service continuity during DoS attacks on routers or routing protocols.', 'acceptance_criteria': 'GIVEN a routing protocol attack or failure;
WHEN the system detects a routing failure;
THEN the system shall automatically degrade service to a minimal viable state and maintain availability for critical services within 5 seconds.'}, {'id': 'SEC-003', 'requirement': 'All routers shall perform protocol syntax and semantics checks to prevent exploitation via malformed or malformed routing messages.', 'rationale': 'RFC 4732 emphasizes that routers must validate protocol messages to prevent attacks that exploit routing protocol vulnerabilities.', 'acceptance_criteria': "GIVEN a malformed routing message;
WHEN it is received by a router;
THEN the router shall reject the message and log the event with a severity level of 'high'."}, {'id': 'SEC-004', 'requirement': 'The system shall isolate router-to-router traffic to prevent amplification attacks and lateral movement during DoS events.', 'rationale': 'Isolating router-to-router traffic, as recommended in RFC 4732, reduces the risk of DoS attacks that exploit routing infrastructure or amplify traffic.', 'acceptance_criteria': 'GIVEN a DoS attack attempting to exploit router-to-router communication;
WHEN the system detects such an attempt;
THEN the traffic shall be isolated and blocked at the router level with a log entry indicating the action.'}]

[{'id': 'SEC-001', 'requirement': 'The router shall identify and categorize legitimate control plane traffic based on known protocols and traffic patterns (e.g., OSPF, BGP, SNMP, NETCONF) to ensure only authorized traffic reaches the control plane.', 'rationale': 'Legitimate control plane traffic is essential for routing and management functions; identifying it enables effective filtering of unwanted traffic.', 'acceptance_criteria': 'GIVEN a router with known control plane traffic patterns;
WHEN traffic is analyzed against a defined set of legitimate protocols;
THEN traffic matching the patterns shall be allowed to reach the control plane, and all other traffic shall be either blocked or rate-limited.'}, {'id': 'SEC-002', 'requirement': 'The router shall deploy a forwarding-plane filter that prevents or rate-limits traffic not specifically identified as legitimate control plane traffic, with a maximum rate limit of 100 packets per second for non-legitimate traffic.', 'rationale': 'The forwarding plane is closer to the line rate hardware, making it more effective for DoS mitigation and reducing the risk of control plane overload.', 'acceptance_criteria': 'GIVEN a high-traffic network environment;
WHEN a packet is received that does not match a legitimate control plane traffic pattern;
THEN the packet shall be rate-limited to no more than 100 packets per second, or blocked, depending on configuration.'}, {'id': 'NON-001', 'requirement': 'The router shall maintain a logging mechanism that records all traffic filtering decisions, including blocked or rate-limited packets, with timestamps and source IP addresses.', 'rationale': 'Logging enables visibility into filtering behavior and supports incident response and auditability.', 'acceptance_criteria': 'GIVEN a filtering event;
WHEN a packet is blocked or rate-limited;
