WHEN they attempt to communicate via TCP/IP;
THEN the communication succeeds without requiring external IP connectivity or gateway mediation.'}, {'id': 'SEC-002', 'requirement': 'No device on the internal network shall be assigned a globally unique IP address or have direct access to the public Internet.', 'rationale': 'To prevent unnecessary routing overhead and reduce exposure to external threats, all devices must operate within a private address space as defined in RFC 1918.', 'acceptance_criteria': 'GIVEN a device on the internal network;
