WHEN a <get-config> RPC is sent to a device;
THEN the device shall respond with a well-formed XML document containing the requested configuration data.'}, {'id': 'FUNC-002', 'category': 'Functional', 'text': 'The system shall support the <edit-config> operation to modify device configuration data, with subtree filtering to limit the scope of changes.', 'rationale': 'RFC 6241 defines <edit-config> as a primary mechanism for updating configurations, and subtree filtering enables precise, targeted modifications.', 'acceptance_criteria': 'GIVEN a configuration change request with a subtree filter;
WHEN the <edit-config> RPC is sent;
THEN only the specified configuration elements shall be modified, and the device shall return a <rpc-reply> with <ok> if successful.'}, {'id': 'NON-001', 'category': 'Non-Functional', 'text': 'The system shall support message pipelining to improve throughput during high-volume configuration operations.', 'rationale': 'RFC 6241 specifies pipelining as a feature that allows multiple RPCs to be sent without waiting for individual responses, improving performance.', 'acceptance_criteria': 'GIVEN a sequence of configuration operations;
