WHEN the configuration is uploaded;
THEN the system shall validate the configuration on all devices and report any inconsistencies.'}]

[{'id': 'SEC-001', 'category': 'Security', 'text': 'The RESTCONF API shall use HTTPS with X.509v3 certificates to ensure confidentiality and integrity of data in transit.', 'rationale': 'As specified in the RFC, HTTPS with X.509v3 certificates is required for authenticated communication between clients and devices, ensuring data confidentiality and integrity.', 'acceptance_criteria': "GIVEN a client attempting to access device data via RESTCONF;
WHEN the connection uses HTTPS;
THEN the data transmitted shall be encrypted using TLS 1.2 or higher, and the server's identity shall be validated using X.509v3 certificates."}, {'id': 'FUNC-001', 'category': 'Functional', 'text': 'The API shall support a root resource discovery endpoint that returns a list of available data and operation resources.', 'rationale': 'The RESTCONF protocol defines a root resource discovery mechanism (Section 3.1) to allow clients to discover available resources without prior knowledge of the data model.', 'acceptance_criteria': 'GIVEN a client sends a GET request to the root resource;
WHEN the server responds;
THEN the response shall include a list of available resources such as {+restconf}/data and {+restconf}/operations.'}, {'id': 'FUNC-002', 'category': 'Functional', 'text': 'The API shall support a GET method to retrieve data from a specific datastore resource, using a URI-encoded data resource identifier.', 'rationale': 'The RESTCONF protocol defines a data resource model (Section 3.4) that allows retrieval of data using a URI-encoded identifier, with support for entity tags and timestamps to prevent edit collisions.', 'acceptance_criteria': 'GIVEN a client sends a GET request to /data/device/config/interface/eth0;
WHEN the device is configured with a YANG model;
