WHEN the receiving host retrieves the SPF record for the domain in the MAIL FROM field;
THEN the host shall evaluate the sending host against the SPF record and return a result of 'Pass', 'Fail', or 'Neutral'."}, {'id': 'SPF-REQ-003', 'type': 'non-functional', 'description': 'The SPF check shall complete within 500 milliseconds to avoid introducing significant latency in email delivery.', 'rationale': 'Ensures timely validation of email messages without impacting delivery performance.', 'acceptance_criteria': 'GIVEN a high-volume email traffic scenario;
WHEN an SPF check is performed;
THEN the check shall complete within 500 milliseconds, measured from the start of DNS lookup to the final result.'}, {'id': 'SPF-REQ-004', 'type': 'security', 'description': "The SPF check shall return a 'Fail' result if the sending host is not authorized by the domain's SPF record, and the receiving host shall reject the message with a proper error code.", 'rationale': 'Enforces domain ownership and prevents spoofed emails from being delivered to recipients.', 'acceptance_criteria': "GIVEN a message from an unauthorized host;
