[{'id': 'SEC-001', 'category': 'Security', 'text': 'All email traffic between Mail User Agents (MUAs) and Mail Submission Servers, as well as between MUAs and Mail Access Servers, shall use Transport Layer Security (TLS) version 1.2 or higher.', 'rationale': 'This aligns with RFC 8314, which recommends TLS 1.2+ for maximum confidentiality and security against known vulnerabilities in older TLS versions.', 'acceptance_criteria': 'GIVEN a mail client connects to a mail server via IMAP or SMTP submission;
WHEN the connection is established;
THEN the TLS handshake shall use TLS version 1.2 or greater, and the connection shall be encrypted end-to-end.'}, {'id': 'SEC-002', 'category': 'Security', 'text': 'All mail servers shall use implicit TLS for POP, IMAP, and SMTP submission, in preference to cleartext connections or STARTTLS negotiations.', 'rationale': 'Implicit TLS provides stronger security by establishing an encrypted connection from the outset, avoiding the risk of a man-in-the-middle attack during the STARTTLS negotiation phase.', 'acceptance_criteria': 'GIVEN a mail client attempts to connect to a mail server on the implicit TLS port;
