Actors/Assets: System components (e.g., servers, databases), backup storage at primary and alternate locations, cryptographic keys.
Functional Concerns: System recovery and reconstitution to a known operational state within defined time and point objectives; transaction recovery for transaction-based systems (e.g., databases).
Non-Functional Concerns: Recovery time objectives (RTO), recovery point objectives (RPO), restoration time periods, system availability, integrity of restored components.
Security Concerns: Cryptographic protection of data at rest in backups; key management; protection of recovery components (e.g., router tables, compilers, system software);
Assumptions: The organization has defined RTO and RPO values; backup data is stored in both primary and alternate locations; recovery operations are supported by automated or manual procedures;
Missing Information: Specific time period for recovery or restoration; whether transaction recovery is required; whether system components are transaction-based; details on key management processes; organizational metrics for recovery and reconstitution.

